miadi-music-measure — the Python that measures music on a Miadi host

  /usr/lib/miadi-music/venv/bin/python3    NumPy, SciPy and Pillow, pinned
  /usr/share/miadi-music/wheels/cp<NN>/    the wheels it is built from, and constraints.txt,
                                           from miadi-music-wheels-cp<NN>

The wheels come in one package per Python: miadi-music-wheels-cp310 (Ubuntu
22.04), -cp311 (Debian 12) and -cp312 (Ubuntu 24.04). Each depends on its
python3, so apt installs only the set this host can use, and each stays under
the apt repository's 100 MB limit.

postinst builds the venv from them with --no-index, using the first Python
with venv (python3, python3.12, python3.11, python3.10) that has a wheels set,
then checks that NumPy and SciPy import together
without a warning and that scipy.signal runs. A wheels package installed,
upgraded or replaced rebuilds the venv (a dpkg trigger), as after a release
upgrade changes python3. Removing the package removes the venv.

Why a venv: on a host where pip put a newer NumPy in /usr/local, the
distribution's SciPy imports with a version warning and is not a supported
pair. This venv reads neither /usr/local nor the distribution's packages.

The pins are in prep/miadi-music-measure.constraints.txt of
jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit packages/miadi/deb.
